    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "One hand position",
      "body": "Play I–V–vi–IV in C without moving your hand: C (C E G), G/B (B D G), Am (A C E) and F/A (A C F). Each change moves one or two fingers a step, and the common tones stay put.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is exactly how band keyboard players play the four chords behind a huge number of songs.",
